    "result_text": "All 263 tests pass, including the 25 in `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe repo already had a duplicate-owner 409 check, but its semantics were wrong \u2014 it only rejected when **last name AND telephone** both matched. The spec requires rejecting when the **telephone alone** is already used by any other owner.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 rewrote `isDuplicateOwner` to scan all owners (`findAllOwners()`) and match on telephone only, dropping the last-name condition. `addOwner` already returns `409 CONFLICT` when this returns true.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`** \u2014 added `createOwnerConflictWhenSameTelephoneDifferentLastName`, which posts a second owner with a different name/address/city but the same telephone and asserts `409`. The existing tests (identical duplicate \u2192 409, same last-name+phone \u2192 409, same last-name different phone \u2192 201) remain valid under the new rule.",
